args:
- description: |
    A comma-separated list of URLs to extract content from.  Each value can be a full URL with protocol or a bare domain; if no protocol is given, http:// or https:// is added automatically, based on the Rasterize integration instance configuration (http:// by default). For example "https://example.com" or "https://a.com,https://b.com,https://c.com".
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: url
  required: true
  type: string
  underlyingargname: url
- defaultvalue: "0"
  description: |
    Time in seconds to wait before extracting content after page load completes. Useful for pages with dynamic content that loads after initial page rendering. If content extraction fails or returns incomplete results, try increasing this value (e.g., 5-10 seconds for slow-loading dynamic content).
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: wait_time
  required: false
  type: number
  underlyingargname: wait_time
- defaultvalue: "180"
  description: |
    Maximum time in seconds to wait for the page to load before timing out. Prevents hanging on slow or unresponsive pages. If you encounter timeout errors, increase this value (e.g., 300 or 600 seconds) for slow-loading pages or pages with heavy content.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: max_page_load_time
  required: false
  type: number
  underlyingargname: max_page_load_time
